Formal additive control baseline is now committed and ordinarily pushed: 9a861d05141bfbf9bdf6465d96392ee047edc408 (includes3636dd6 plus reviewed authority-type guard). Native user-authorized P0 continues. Read packages/contracts/process_control/README.md, schema/helpers/generated OpenAPI, docs/adr/0002-process-evidence-and-presentation.md §§2–5, current decisions/full applicable R36/R51/R52/R58/A16/A30/A31/A38/A42/A43 and scoped AUDIO-14. Read exact task P0-09/current control boundary at that SHA; use git show first, preserve work, then coordinate a normal merge without reset. v1 and capture0.2.0 bytes are frozen; control is separate0.2.1, capability process.control.v0.2.1/scope process:control.

Implement the smallest internal persisted registry/resolver slice in services/api/** and existing module tests/docs/verification/backend/**; Backend alone owns any additive migration. Reuse existing actor transaction and CaptureArchive:
- explicit currently owned device-session membership with revision plus account authorization generation;
- new stream registration only through an exact-ID one-use trusted internal start decision pinned to current generations; invalidate affected pending grants on stop/revoke, no page/request booleans or public grant-creation endpoint;
- durable stop / seal_stop / withdraw, no old-ID resume; known boundary from an independent trusted producer stop fact and >=actual committed same-stream sequence floor, never copy request into trusted proof; unknown stays blocked;
- atomic idempotency: fresh authority/membership/generations first, exact replay before CAS/start consumption, return CURRENT state (stopped/withdrawn), never cached live. Changed body/key conflict; foreign/deleted/absent identities indistinguishable, no resurrection;
- resolver into unchanged capture0.2.0 in same transaction with current source/version ownership and stop/delete fences through commit. Keep independent streams scoped; no global microphone/single-stream assertion.

Focused portable tests plus new real PostgreSQL checks on existing dedicated instance: delayed uncommitted registration after revoke/regrant, both lifecycle/capture commit orders, membership changes, repeat command vs stale fresh CAS, unknown→sealed boundary, zero only truly empty, fresh restart predecessor/gap, stop/withdraw replay and deletion. Avoid re-running completed17a7dc8 batch as new work. Report measured DB lock ordering separately from portable results.

Read newly arrived QA bd79ca4 report/test module via git show. It confirms old internal capture slice but raises low AUTH-01 collection type issues, lock-held repeated batch validation, and shared v1 artifact deletion/pin issues. In this control/resolver segment reject malformed collection types at your existing CaptureArchive resolver boundary as well as using the new strict ControlAuthority; no shared contract byte edits. Keep artifact sharing/upload inactive until its explicit deletion/pin rule and typed contract; a mere pending capture reference does not prove ownership of independent user ink. Report concrete adjacent conflicts to lead; do not silently redesign the entire artifact store or add a fast path that skips validation. Lead retains that shared follow-up.

No HTTP activation, public start-grant API, typed upload, attempt/disclosure/export, provider/device/runtime/model/permission change in this segment. Return committed implementation, focused test commands/results, actual migration/DB evidence and unverified conditions via one substantive native reply. No acknowledgement loop or duplicate ingestion implementation.
